Q: Getting a random value from an enum class variable A: <p>I would add to each enum where you need it the method <code>getRundom()</code> for example:</p>
<pre><code>public enum WeekDay {
    MONDAY, TUESDAY, WEDNESDAY, THURSDAY, FRIDAY, SATURDAY, SUNDAY;

   private Random random = new Random();
   public static WeekDay getRandom() {
      return values()[random.nextInt(values().length()]);
   }
}
</code></pre>
<p>After that anywhere you need it just use</p>
<pre><code>WeekDay.getRandom();
</code></pre>
<p>And so on to each enum where you need it</p>
